17:["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"The CMS-1500 is the standard claim form for professional services — physician and outpatient practice billing. Institutional claims from hospitals use the UB-04, also called the CMS-1450. Almost all claims are transmitted electronically rather than on paper: the CMS-1500 corresponds to the 837P transaction, and the UB-04 to the 837I."}]
18:["$","p","2",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Even when you never see the paper form, its field structure is what the electronic transaction carries and what every billing system's screens are modeled on. Knowing the fields is knowing the claim."}]
